      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After some tests, i have conclusion:\n\n- if world has no function \"Postprocessing layer\" on Main Camera, and you use handheld camera, all photos will pixelated, no smoothing applied.\n\n- if world has Postprocessing layer on Main Camera, it doesn't matter if function is active or disabled, we can see smoothing is enabled on handheld camera.\n\nGood news the \"photobooth\" cameras (extra camera in world), we can see smoothing is enabled on the world cameras, no matter function is there.\n\nIt's only the handheld camera is affected, depends on if function is added to Main Camera or not.\n\nWorld creators should add just only function to Main Camera to solve it. Set it on Water layer as example. Then there is no problem with handheld camera.\n\nThis problem was not found in 2019-client. After update to 2022-client, the smoothing function in handheld camera seems removed or bugged.\n\nOnly polygons are effected. Textures are fine. But edges of cubes or meshes are not smooth, it's just not great to see it. All avatars and models are affected.\n\nUPDATE: After many testing, i found out now what makes smooth effect possible on handheld camera:\n\n- the world must have Main Camera linked as Reference Camera in VRC World\n\n- add Postprocessing Layer (function) to Main Camera.\n\nThat is it. So world creators, don't forget it, or people cannot make nice smooth photos in your worlds, all will pixelated due missing MSAA filter.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
